// Title: Which VMs and subnets talk to Azure Storage public IPs
// Purpose: Find the clients of storage accounts that you want to put behind private endpoints (before blocking public access).
// Source table(s): NTAIpDetails, NTANetAnalytics
// Parameters to edit: Lookback.
// Notes/traps: NTAIpDetails maps IPs to public service names (PublicIpDetails == 'AzureStorage'). Query 1
//          groups per source VM and subnet, query 2 per flow-log target with GB transferred.
//          Flow logs only see traffic that goes out through the VNet, not traffic from outside Azure.
//
// --- Query 1: per source VM / subnet
let Lookback = 24h;
let StorageIps = NTAIpDetails
| where TimeGenerated > ago(Lookback)
| where PublicIpDetails == 'AzureStorage'
| distinct Ip;
NTANetAnalytics
| where TimeGenerated > ago(Lookback)
| where SubType == 'FlowLog'
| where DestIp in (StorageIps)
| summarize Flows = sum(AllowedOutFlows) + sum(AllowedInFlows),
            Denied = sum(DeniedOutFlows) + sum(DeniedInFlows),
            MB = round((sum(BytesSrcToDest) + sum(BytesDestToSrc)) / 1024.0 / 1024.0, 1),
            Ports = make_set(DestPort, 5)
    by SrcVm, SrcSubnet
| order by Flows desc
| take 25
